2577009784,"type":"genre","name":"ballad","n":1}],"labels":[],"album_labels":[],"own_scenes":[],"scenes":[],"book_tracks":[],"mentions":[],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":"Critic Robert Hull's Disparaging Remarks (1975)","body":"In a misogynistic assessment from 1975, critic Robert Hull dismissed Ann Murray as \"Ugly\" in a crude ranking of female singers he would like \"to sit in your lap.\" \"Ann Murray, Ugly\"","year":1975,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 40 - Honestly Loving Olivia Newton-John","url":"https://seventies.libsyn.com/ep-40-honestly-loving-olivia-newton-john"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Duet Performance with Chris Christopherson (1981)","body":"While initially released as a solo record, Ann Murray did perform \"Could I Have This Dance\" as a duet with Chris Christopherson on her 1981 TV Christmas Special. This fulfilled, in part, her original vision for the song as a duet. \"She did sing it with Chris Christopherson on her TV Christmas Special in 1981.\"","year":1981,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 50 - The Travolta Trilogy","url":"https://www.ftr70.com/"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Premature Album Inclusion","body":"So confident in the song's potential, Murray included \"Could I Have This Dance\" on her greatest hits album even before it was officially released as a single. This decision proved to be prescient given the song's eventual success. \"She was feeling so optimistic about this song that she included it on her greatest hits record before it was ever released as a single.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 50 - The Travolta Trilogy","url":"https://www.ftr70.com/"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Touring with Jerry Seinfeld","body":"As a young comedian, Jerry Seinfeld worked on the road with Ann Murray, alongside Andy Williams. \"He's been working on the road with Ann Murray and Andy Williams.\"","year":n